<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KhaozEngine.Gpu.Vulkan</PackageId>
    <!-- Shared engine version line: <KhaozEngineVersion> in Directory.Build.props. -->
    <Version>$(KhaozEngineVersion)</Version>
    <!-- net10.0 with NO OS suffix, NO [SupportedOSPlatformGuard] and NO NoInlining bodies, which is decision
         V-P1. Vulkan is not a Windows API: the same managed code runs on Windows and Linux, the loader is found
         at runtime, and a machine without one fails the functional probe and routes through the existing
         fallback. The whole CA1416 apparatus KhaozEngine.Gpu.D3D11 needs has no analogue here, so its absence is
         a simplification rather than an omission. Nobody should add it back by analogy with the D3D11 package. -->
    <!-- Vulkan's structures carry raw pointer arrays as a matter of ABI (VkRenderingInfo.pColorAttachments,
         VkDependencyInfo's three barrier arrays, VkSemaphoreWaitInfo's parallel semaphore and value arrays), and
         the debug-utils messenger takes a function pointer. There is no safe spelling of any of that, so this
         backend is unsafe by construction rather than by choice, unlike the ONE ring copy that earns the flag in
         KhaozEngine.Gpu.D3D11. Same flag KhaozEngine.Gpu, Render2D and Render3D already carry. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Description>Engine-owned native Vulkan backend for the KhaozEngine.Gpu seam (carried by the KhaozEngine.Game2D and KhaozEngine.Game3D umbrellas since 18.0.0, along with its two siblings, because KhaozEngine.Gpu builds no device of its own any more). Targets net10.0 with no OS suffix and no platform guards, because Vulkan is not a Windows API and the assembly loads harmlessly anywhere. Binds Vulkan through Silk.NET.Vulkan on the same 2.23.0 line the windowing, input and audio stacks already pin. BUILT, CONTINUOUSLY EXERCISED, AND THE DEFAULT ON LINUX SINCE 17.40.0: KhaozEngineVulkan.Register(), the functional machine-capability probe, HEADLESS AND WINDOWED device creation (one refcounted VkInstance, features enabled by name, a device-loss latch and the KE_VULKAN_VALIDATION pump), the completion timeline, the block memory allocator, the command list with its full recording content, the uniform ring, the RESOURCE FACTORY (buffers, textures with every image view made eagerly and a canonical resting layout, samplers, staging maps and a device-owned setup command buffer that keeps texture creation off the queue), the descriptors and the bind flush, dynamic rendering, the shader path, the pipelines, the swapchain, the barrier tracker and the capability, counter and diagnostics reads are all real. No member of the package refuses by naming a work-breakdown row any more. Spec: docs/design/VULKAN-NATIVE-BACKEND-DESIGN-2026-08-05.md.</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Gpu/KhaozEngine.Gpu.csproj" />
    <!-- The engine logger, for the one line the support probe writes when it answers no. Declared explicitly
         rather than ridden transitively through KhaozEngine.Gpu, the same way KhaozEngine.Gpu.D3D11 declares it:
         a backend that logs should say so in its own project file. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="../KhaozEngine.Diagnostics/KhaozEngine.Diagnostics.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The Vulkan binding (V-P2). Pinned centrally in Directory.Packages.props to the 2.23.0 Silk.NET line the
         engine already runs everywhere else. The two extension packages are where the KHR and EXT entry points
         live in this binding: KHR carries the swapchain and the three platform surface extensions, EXT carries
         the debug-utils messenger the validation knob pumps. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Silk.NET.Vulkan" />
    <PackageReference Include="Silk.NET.Vulkan.Extensions.KHR" />
    <PackageReference Include="Silk.NET.Vulkan.Extensions.EXT" />
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.Render.Tests" />
    <!-- The uniform ring's SEMANTIC tests are shared with the Direct3D 11 backend (decisions V-P5, V-T6): one
         internal test-only interface and BOTH adapters live in KhaozEngine.TestSupport.Gpu, which is
         IsPackable=false and ships nothing, so V-P4's no-shared-PRODUCTION-home rule is untouched. The Direct3D 11
         package carries the same grant, added by the same row. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="KhaozEngine.TestSupport.Gpu" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
